00:42:08.423 --> 00:42:09.270
- [Kip ] Well, that's a great question.

00:42:09.270 --> 00:42:10.103
So I,

00:42:11.880 --> 00:42:15.010
I basically was interested
in ecology for a long time

00:42:15.010 --> 00:42:20.010
and I was studying abroad in Costa Rica.

00:42:20.120 --> 00:42:21.640
Which is a very tropical area.

00:42:21.640 --> 00:42:23.213
And there's a type of ant
that lives there called

00:42:23.213 --> 00:42:24.163
a leaf cutter.

00:42:25.396 --> 00:42:26.500
And I encourage you guys to look them up

00:42:26.500 --> 00:42:27.333
if you're interested.

00:42:27.333 --> 00:42:29.630
But basically what they do,
is they will cut little bits

00:42:29.630 --> 00:42:31.000
off of leaves

00:42:31.000 --> 00:42:34.720
and they will carry them in
lines that look like highways,

00:42:34.720 --> 00:42:37.330
from the plant they're carrying
it from back to their nest.

00:42:37.330 --> 00:42:41.100
And basically I was walking
around and I just realized

00:42:41.100 --> 00:42:43.000
that I was crossing an ant highway

00:42:43.890 --> 00:42:47.740
with all these ants carrying
leaves on their backs.

00:42:47.740 --> 00:42:49.820
And I, I leaned down to look at them.

00:42:49.820 --> 00:42:51.540
And then I noticed that on the leaves

00:42:51.540 --> 00:42:52.990
there were little bitty ants.

00:42:53.870 --> 00:42:55.910
Well on the leaves they
were just like half the size

00:42:55.910 --> 00:42:58.000
or even the third of the
size of their sisters.

00:42:58.000 --> 00:43:00.630
Maybe I can find a picture
of this to send also.

00:43:00.630 --> 00:43:03.990
But she, the little ant riding the leaf,

00:43:03.990 --> 00:43:07.603
was cleaning the leaf
while it was being carried.

00:43:08.740 --> 00:43:10.130
And I just found this fascinating cause

00:43:10.130 --> 00:43:12.020
that that's what inspired
me to study ants.

00:43:12.020 --> 00:43:16.533
And I haven't been able
to, to kick the habit yet.

